      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-26T06:04:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For \"copy_cord_prereqs is needed to create/copy an ssh key from the config to head node to work around password-auth SSH\" do we have a Jira ticket, so we know that we still have a problem to fix? If not, shouldn\u0027t this just be the default behavior?\n\nFor \"skipTags is MaaS... something?  I\u0027m not up on what they\u0027re all for, and it\u0027s not best practice.\" this shouldn\u0027t be mandatory. As long as we clearly say to users where the generated passwords are, it should be fine not having it. I would in that case like to put it as one of the optional (commented) params\n\nI understand it\u0027s needed, but why the user should bother to see a default param, if we can possibly just copying it using the address of the head node - already inserted?",
